{"abstract":[{"text":"Combine JSON documents symmetrically, with overrides, or via JSON Merge Patch.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON/MergingJSON"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"DynamicJSON"}],"role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Merging JSON Values"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"DynamicJSON","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" offers three ways of merging JSON values, each suited for a different purpose.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Symmetrical-merge","level":3,"text":"Symmetrical merge","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The method ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON/JSON/isRefinement(of:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" defines a relationship between two JSON values.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"a.isRefinement(of: b)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is true if","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"both ","type":"text"},{"code":"a","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"b","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are JSON values of the same type,","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"if ","type":"text"},{"code":"a","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"b","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are arrays, they have the same length ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"a[i].isRefinement(of: b[i])","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"holds for every i ∈ [0; ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":"[,","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"if ","type":"text"},{"code":"a","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"b","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are objects, for every member ","type":"text"},{"code":"m","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of ","type":"text"},{"code":"b","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with value ","type":"text"},{"code":"b[m]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", there is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"member ","type":"text"},{"code":"m","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of ","type":"text"},{"code":"a","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with value ","type":"text"},{"code":"a[m]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" such that ","type":"text"},{"code":"a[m].isRefinement(of: b[m])","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"for all other types, ","type":"text"},{"code":"a","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"b","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are the same, i.e. ","type":"text"},{"code":"a == b","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Intuitively: whenever it is possible to read a value at a given location from ","type":"text"},{"code":"b","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", it is also","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"possible to read a value at that location from ","type":"text"},{"code":"a","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the value read from ","type":"text"},{"code":"a","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refinement of the value read from ","type":"text"},{"code":"b","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let a = try JSON(string: #\"\"\"","  {","    \"a\": [1, { \"b\": 2 }],","    \"c\": { \"d\": [{}] }","  }","\"\"\"#)","let b = try JSON(string: #\"\"\"","  {","    \"a\": [1, { \"b\": 2, \"e\": 4 }],","    \"c\": { \"d\": [{\"f\": 5}] }","  }","\"\"\"#)","b.isRefinement(of: a) ⇒ true"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON/JSON/merging(value:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" merges two values ","type":"text"},{"code":"a","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"b","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" into the “smallest” value that is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refinement of both. If no such value exists, the method returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let c = try JSON(string: #\"\"\"","  { \"a\": [1, {\"e\": 8}],","    \"c\": {\"f\": \"hello\"},","    \"g\": 9 }","\"\"\"#)","a.merging(value: c)","⇒","{","  \"a\": [1, { \"b\": 2, \"e\": 8 }],","  \"c\": { \"d\": [{}], \"f\": \"hello\" },","  \"g\": 9","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Non-existing values are added to the result and overlapping values are merged where possible.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"If two values cannot be merged, the result is ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Overriding-merge","level":3,"text":"Overriding merge","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON/JSON/overriding(with:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" merges two values differently: the argument overrides values of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the receiver wherever a symmetrical merge would fail. Arrays do not need to have the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"length. The result has the length of the longer array, and elements available in both are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"combined with ","type":"text"},{"code":"overriding(with:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let d = try JSON(string: #\"\"\"","  {","    \"a\": [1, { \"e\": 2 }, 3],","    \"c\": { \"d\": \"hello\" },","    \"f\": 5","  }","\"\"\"#)","a.overriding(with: d)","⇒","{","  \"a\": [1, { \"b\": 2, \"e\": 2 }, 3],","  \"c\": { \"d\": \"hello\" },","  \"f\": 5","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"JSON-Merge-Patch","level":3,"text":"JSON Merge Patch","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON/JSON/merging(patch:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" implements ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"JSON Merge Patch","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" as defined by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7396/","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". A merge patch document describes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changes to a target document using a syntax that closely mimics the document being modified.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Members of the patch that do not appear in the target are added, members that do appear are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"replaced, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values in the patch remove the corresponding members from the target.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Objects are merged recursively; all other kinds of values are replaced by the patch.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let target = try JSON(string: #\"{\"a\": \"b\", \"c\": {\"d\": \"e\", \"f\": \"g\"}}\"#)","let patch = try JSON(string: #\"{\"a\": \"z\", \"c\": {\"f\": null}}\"#)","target.merging(patch: patch)","⇒","{\"a\": \"z\", \"c\": {\"d\": \"e\"}}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The implementation does not mutate the existing value. It constructs a new value by merging","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the old one with the patch document.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON":{"abstract":[{"text":"Represent, query, mutate, merge, and validate generic JSON values.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"DynamicJSON","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/dynamicjson"},"doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON/JSON/isRefinement(of:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Returns true if this JSON value is a refinement of ","type":"text"},{"code":"other","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A JSON array ","type":"text"},{"code":"lhs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refinement of another JSON value ","type":"text"},{"code":"rhs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if ","type":"text"},{"code":"rhs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is also an array of equal length","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"such that every element ","type":"text"},{"code":"lhs[i]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a refinement of ","type":"text"},{"code":"rhs[i]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A JSON object ","type":"text"},{"code":"lhs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refinement of another JSON value ","type":"text"},{"code":"rhs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if ","type":"text"},{"code":"rhs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is also an object such that for every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"member ","type":"text"},{"code":"m","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of ","type":"text"},{"code":"rhs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"lhs[m]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a refinement of ","type":"text"},{"code":"rhs[m]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Any other JSON value ","type":"text"},{"code":"lhs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a refinement of another JSON value ","type":"text"},{"code":"rhs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if ","type":"text"},{"code":"lhs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is equal to ","type":"text"},{"code":"rhs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isRefinement"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11DynamicJSON0B0O","text":"JSON"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"}],"identifier":"doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON/JSON/isRefinement(of:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"isRefinement(of:)","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/dynamicjson/json/isrefinement(of:)"},"doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON/JSON/merging(patch:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Merges this JSON value with the given JSON value ","type":"text"},{"code":"patch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" recursively. Objects are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"merged key by key with values from ","type":"text"},{"code":"patch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" overriding values of the object represented","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by this JSON value. All other types of JSON values are not merged and ","type":"text"},{"code":"patch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" overrides","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this JSON value. This implements the following algorithm as specified in RFC 7396 on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"JSON Merge Patch.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"merging"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"patch"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11DynamicJSON0B0O","text":"JSON"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11DynamicJSON0B0O","text":"JSON"}],"identifier":"doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON/JSON/merging(patch:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"merging(patch:)","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/dynamicjson/json/merging(patch:)"},"doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON/JSON/merging(value:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Merges two JSON values symmetrically, combining matching arrays and objects. If","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"incompatible values are to be matched, then ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is returned. If this method","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"succeeds, the resulting value is a refinement of the two merged values as defined","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by ","type":"text"},{"code":"isRefinement(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"merging"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"value"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11DynamicJSON0B0O","text":"JSON"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11DynamicJSON0B0O","text":"JSON"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"identifier":"doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON/JSON/merging(value:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"merging(value:)","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/dynamicjson/json/merging(value:)"},"doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON/JSON/overriding(with:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Merges two JSON values, combining matching arrays and objects. If incompatible values","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are to be matched, then the value defined by ","type":"text"},{"code":"rhs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" overrides the value of ","type":"text"},{"code":"lhs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"As opposed to method ","type":"text"},{"code":"merging(value:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", combining arrays does not require the arrays to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be of the same length. The resulting array has always the length of the longest of the two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arrays and individual elements are combined using ","type":"text"},{"code":"overriding(with:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whenever two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements are available.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"overriding"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"with"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11DynamicJSON0B0O","text":"JSON"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11DynamicJSON0B0O","text":"JSON"}],"identifier":"doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON/JSON/overriding(with:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"overriding(with:)","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/dynamicjson/json/overriding(with:)"},"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7396/":{"identifier":"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7396/","title":"RFC 7396","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"RFC 7396","type":"text"}],"type":"link","url":"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7396/"}},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Merging","identifiers":["doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON/JSON/isRefinement(of:)","doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON/JSON/merging(value:)","doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON/JSON/overriding(with:)","doc://DynamicJSON/documentation/DynamicJSON/JSON/merging(patch:)"],"title":"Merging"}],"variants":[{"paths":["/documentation/dynamicjson/mergingjson"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}]}